{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeDMzjahGtdw2G2izP8pm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`git add/commit/push` are denied to me by project policy; the loop driver commits from a prepared message file. Writing it."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":782,"cache_read_input_tokens":182337,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":782},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43498f3c-c9c5-40d9-b79a-d6b785466892","uuid":"a39fe49d-2aa5-4ece-9ee1-42274d686a3c","timestamp":"2026-08-20T04:23:32.255Z","request_id":"req_011CeDMzic9qm6EqmYhHJxkR"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeDMzjahGtdw2G2izP8pm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ft8AeQo1HtJ6X8TWVVmE77","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/patrickd/deepseek-v4-flash-0731-cuda/evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_0p4.txt","content":"0.4 attributed the context term: 0.2 never varied context, and the biggest carrier is a recompute\n\nWHAT WAS MEASURED. One server load, seqmax 16384, DSV4_DPROF=1, 145 steady-state verify steps\nat four context depths from 772 to 12,406, every step tagged with the context it was taken at.\nPer-mark least squares against context, with standard errors, width held fixed:\n\n  mark                     ms/1000 ctx (b|VB)    ms @ ctx 768   @ 12,288   share\n  STEP (verify + draft)     6.969 +/- 0.112        126.3          203.9     100%\n    draft:main_kv           3.867 +/- 0.001          3.30          47.87     55%\n    ATTENTION               3.173 +/- 0.109         52.3           87.4      46%\n      cattn:indexer         1.515 +/- 0.029          5.80          22.20     22%\n        i:topk              0.872 +/- 0.021          2.58          13.47   12.5%\n        i:score             0.644 +/- 0.018          0.92           6.58      9%\n      cattn:sparse          0.709 +/- 0.050         11.00          21.17     10%\n    MoE                    -0.079 +/- 0.029          flat           flat      ~0\n    every dense GEMM        within 1 SE of zero\n\nThe per-mark slopes sum exactly to the step slope, so nothing in the step is unattributed. The\ninstrument reproduces the fit it exists to explain: 0.3's wall-clock b was 7.362 +/- 0.370, and\n7.029 +/- 0.28 width-controlled, against 6.969 +/- 0.112 here -- 0.9% apart. The wall-clock legs\nalso reproduce 0.3 point for point (214.7/215.9 vs 215.33 ms/forward at ctx 12.3k; 181.5/182.5 vs\n179.2 at 6.1k; 160.8/162.6 vs 160.5 at 3.1k), so DSV4_DPROF costs nothing measurable and this\nprofiles the shipped cost, not an instrumented one. tau 1.52-1.91 across the legs, in band with\n0.3's 1.63-1.97 on the same corpus.\n\nWHAT IT MEANS, FIRST: 0.2 DID NOT MEASURE TWO CONTEXTS. It measured the same context twice.\nsrc/decode.cu takes its prompt from argv[2]; DSV4_PROMPTS_FILE only appends prompts 1..N and the\nbase-AR and K-sweep paths both run prompt 0. Both 0.2 runs passed a 2-id argv[2], so both logs say\n\"prefill 1 positions\", \"step 0 pos 1\", \"prompt=0 s=2\", and both emitted the identical 24 tokens\n223 643 27 15 397 5029 515 260 ... The labels \"ctx 480\" and \"ctx 3000\" were seqmax, which is sized\nfrom the longest prompt in the FILE (480+24+7+8=519, 3000+24+7+8=3039) -- an allocation, not a\ncontext. Two runs of the same computation at ctx 1..9, reported as a 6x context sweep. That is the\nentire evidence on which 1.2 and 1.5 were retired.\n\nSECOND: 1.2 AND 1.5 ARE UN-RETIRED AND THE NUMBERS WERE OFF BY TWO ORDERS OF MAGNITUDE. 0.2 gave\ni:topk 0.10 ms and i:score 0.02 ms. At ctx 12,288 they are 13.47 ms and 6.58 ms -- 135x and 330x --\nand together they carry 1.52 of the 6.97 ms/1000. They grow because they are O(context) by\nconstruction and 0.2 ran them at context 9.\n\nTHIRD, AND LARGER THAN EITHER: THE DRAFT SIDE HAD NEVER BEEN TIMED AT ALL. Every dprof mark in this\nrepo lived in the verify stack, so dprof_report's TOTAL has only ever described part of a decode\nstep. src/engine.cu calls dspark_main_kv NSTAGE=3 times per step over the full ctxlen -- a\nfrom-scratch fp8 GEMM + rmsnorm + rope + quant over EVERY position in the context, redone on every\ntoken. 47.87 ms at ctx 12,288, the largest single row in the step, 55% of the whole context term,\nR^2 1.000 against context. It is not noisy, it is arithmetic. main_x rows are written once and\nnever rewritten (dspark_main_x writes exactly the acc+1 committed positions and cpos advances past\nthem), and every stage of dspark_main_kv is row-independent, so caching the prefix and recomputing\nonly the committed tail is BIT-EXACT, not approximate. That is the new ladder item 1.0 and the next\niteration takes it.\n\nFOURTH: TERM B IS NOT A BYTES PROBLEM. MoE is flat with width held (-0.079 +/- 0.029 per 1000);\nits apparent -0.38 uncontrolled is a width artifact. Every dense GEMM is flat, including\ncattn:ogroup at 15.8 ms. At ctx 6592 Term B's byte floor is 0.509 ms/forward against ~43 ms\nmeasured, still ~85x off roofline. What is left is serial and redundant work: one recompute and\none selection sort.\n\nINSTRUMENTS, all named before they were built and all of which paid.\n  src/engine.cu now calls dprof_report once per verify, tagged with context. It had called\n    dprof_init since the marks were written and NEVER reported -- so every mark the server ever\n    recorded was discarded, which is why the only profiles that existed came from decode.cu's\n    argv[2]-length K-sweep. Nothing numeric changed: every added call is dprof_begin/end, which\n    returns on !g_dprof_on, and the report is behind DSV4_DPROF. Four CPU gates pass in preflight.\n  include/dprof.h + kernels/dprof.cu: three draft-side ids, placed after DP_ARGMAX so they print as\n    their own rows and do not enter TOTAL, which keeps every historical table comparable.\n  tools/dprof_ctx.py: fits the ladder's own linear model per mark with standard errors, because\n    once a mark is flat R^2 is the wrong statistic and the question is whether an interval covers\n    zero. Drops verify=0, which is not a steady-state step (always VB=7, follows a rewind_to,\n    median 219.5 ms against ~160) and was worth 0.9 ms/1000 of spurious negative MoE slope.\n  tools/decode_fit_probe.py: --targets/--no-control, so 0.3's default sweep and --report are\n    unchanged while 0.4 drives a shorter point list.\n  scripts/dprof_ctx_run.sh: detached, health-gated, arms a memguard run_server.sh does not, fails\n    loudly if the loader dies rather than sweeping a dead engine, and REFUSES to run a binary older\n    than the sources it must describe. Named in detach_audit.sh in this commit, per CLAUDE.md.\n\nNO KERNEL CHANGED IN 0.3 OR 0.4. Two consecutive measurement iterations; the ladder says to declare\nthat and it is declared in the entry. Four of the first five items have now been instruments. The\nwhole context term is attributed with error bars and there is nothing left to measure before\nbuilding, so the ladder now reads: the next four items are all kernel changes and 0.4 is the last\ninstrument this phase gets.\n\nONE OPEN LEAD, RECORDED AND NOT CHASED. At ctx 6144, at the same verify width VB=2 and the same\ncontext, 18 steps ran q:wq_a at 1.71 ms and 17 at 5.47 ms, with cattn:compress splitting the same\nway (0.05 vs 2.50). A 3.2x swing in one fp8 GEMM at fixed shape is not explained by width or\ncontext and is flat in context, so it does not touch this attribution -- but cattn:q_proj is 14.6 ms\nof every step. Filed as 1.8, correctness first: find out which mode is right.\n\nEvidence: evidence/decode_loop/dprof_ctx_0p4.txt (the attribution), server_0p4.log (145 tables),\ndprof/postfix.sweep.jsonl (8 legs), dprof_ctx_run.log, build_server_0p4.log.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":782,"cache_read_input_tokens":182337,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":782},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43498f3c-c9c5-40d9-b79a-d6b785466892","uuid":"d06e36f4-c0fc-4ebd-b4e8-8a2db10298b0","timestamp":"2026-08-20T04:24:08.121Z","request_id":"req_011CeDMzic9qm6EqmYhHJxkR"}
