{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeDN6AUJDhnmpnzFSmzC7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. One ladder item, 0.4, complete.\n\n## What I measured\n\nOne server load, `DSV4_DPROF=1`, 145 steady-state verify steps across four context depths (772 → 12,406), every step tagged with its context. Per-mark least squares with standard errors, verify width held fixed:\n\n| mark | ms per 1000 ctx | @ ctx 768 | @ 12,288 | share |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **STEP (verify+draft)** | **6.969 ± 0.112** | 126.3 | 203.9 | 100 % |\n| `draft:main_kv` | **3.867 ± 0.001** | 3.30 | **47.87** | **55 %** |\n| `ATTENTION` | 3.173 ± 0.109 | 52.3 | 87.4 | 46 % |\n| ⤷ `i:topk` | 0.872 ± 0.021 | 2.58 | **13.47** | 12.5 % |\n| ⤷ `i:score` | 0.644 ± 0.018 | 0.92 | **6.58** | 9 % |\n| ⤷ `cattn:sparse` | 0.709 ± 0.050 | 11.00 | 21.17 | 10 % |\n| `MoE`, every dense GEMM | ≈ 0 (within 1 SE) | flat | flat | ~0 |\n\nPer-mark slopes sum exactly to the step slope. The instrument reproduces 0.3's wall-clock fit to 0.9 % (6.969 ± 0.112 vs 7.029 ± 0.28), and the legs reproduce it point for point, so `DSV4_DPROF` costs nothing measurable. tau 1.52–1.91, in band.\n\n## What it means\n\n**0.2 never varied context.** `src/decode.cu` takes its prompt from `argv[2]`; `DSV4_PROMPTS_FILE` only appends prompts 1..N and both measured paths run prompt 0. Both 0.2 runs passed a 2-id `argv[2]` — both logs say `prefill 1 positions`, `step 0 pos 1`, `prompt=0 s=2`, and both emitted the identical 24 tokens. \"ctx 480\" and \"ctx 3000\" were `seqmax` (480+24+7+8=519, 3000+24+7+8=3039), an allocation, not a context. Two runs of the same computation at ctx 1–9, reported as a 6× sweep — and that is the whole evidence that retired 1.2 and 1.5.\n\n**1.2 and 1.5 are un-retired**, off by 135× and 330× respectively.\n\n**A larger item than either was found because the draft side had never been timed.** Every dprof mark lived in the verify stack. `dspark_main_kv` runs `NSTAGE=3` times per step over the *full* `ctxlen` — a from-scratch fp8 GEMM + rmsnorm + rope + quant over every position, redone every token. 47.87 ms at ctx 12,288, R² 1.000. `main_x` rows are immutable once committed and every stage is row-independent, so caching the prefix is **bit-exact**. Filed as item **1.0** — the next iteration's kernel change.\n\nTerm B is not a bytes problem: at ctx 6592 its byte floor is 0.509 ms/forward against ~43 ms measured. It is one recompute and one selection sort.\n\n## Housekeeping\n\nNo kernel changed in 0.3 or 0.4 — two consecutive measurement iterations, declared at the top of the entry as the ladder requires. Ladder now states 0.4 is the last instrument this phase gets; the next four items are all kernel changes. Nothing numeric changed (all added calls return on `!g_dprof_on`); all six CPU gates pass, nothing resident, 107 GiB free. New stage `dprof_ctx_run.sh` is registered in `detach_audit.sh` in the same commit.\n\n`git add/commit/push` are denied to me by `.claude/settings.json`, so per the established convention I left `evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_0p4.txt` for `scripts/decode_loop.sh` to commit and push on the iteration's behalf.\n\nOne open lead recorded but not chased (filed as 1.8): at ctx 6144 and the same VB=2, `q:wq_a` is cleanly bimodal at 1.71 vs 5.47 ms. Flat in context, so it does not touch this attribution — but `cattn:q_proj` is 14.6 ms of every step."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1356,"cache_read_input_tokens":189887,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1356},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43498f3c-c9c5-40d9-b79a-d6b785466892","uuid":"3c296cb5-224b-48bd-a3b8-9fbef2a5500c","timestamp":"2026-08-20T04:25:00.910Z","request_id":"req_011CeDN68fei1B7Af6VBbpcm"}
